# The DEV platform stack (network, RDS, cluster, ALB, shared IAM, OIDC provider). Deployed
# once from a laptop with admin — NOT by any repo's pipeline. dev owns the account-global
# OIDC provider. GhcrSecretArn is the hand-created ghcr.io pull secret (see infra/README.md).
EnvironmentName=dev
AllowedCidr=0.0.0.0/0
# STUCK ON micro, and it is a hard constraint rather than a choice.
#
# max_connections is derived from instance MEMORY (DBInstanceClassMemory/12582880), so
# micro's 1 GiB gives exactly 60 — MEASURED on the live instance, not read off the formula.
# That is the ceiling every service on this platform shares, and exceeding it kills a module
# in Liquibase with 'Too many connections', which reads as a broken module rather than as an
# exhausted budget nobody was counting.
#
# db.t4g.small would double it to ~127. It was tried on 2026-07-27 and REFUSED:
#   "This instance size isn't available with free plan accounts."
# The stack rolled back cleanly with no data loss. Upgrading the AWS account plan is the
# only way to this lever.
#
# So the budget is enforced on the OTHER side instead — small connection pools, sized in
# infra/README.md § Connection budget. Do not raise a pool without doing that arithmetic.
DbInstanceClass=db.t4g.micro
DbAllocatedStorage=20
CreateOidcProvider=Yes
ExistingOidcProviderArn=
GhcrSecretArn=arn:aws:secretsmanager:ap-southeast-1:192404871113:secret:neobank/ghcr-IPETv3
